A measurement of the branching fractions for the $\mathcal{B}^0	oho^+\ell^- ar{
u}_\ell$ and $\Upsilon(4S)	o\mathcal{B}^0\ell^- ar{
u}_\ell	o\mathcal{B}^0	oho^0\ell^- ar{
u}_\ell$ decays, where $\ell$ represents an electron or a muon, was conducted using a data set collected by the Belle II experiment. The corresponding integrated luminosity was approximately 50 inverse femtobarns. The findings indicate that the branching fractions for the $\mathcal{B}^0	oho^+\ell^- ar{
u}_\ell$ and $\mathcal{B}^0	oho^0\ell^- ar{
u}_\ell$ decays are $1.18\pm0.25\pm0.04\%$ and $0.51\pm0.12\pm0.02\%$, respectively. The primary source of systematic uncertainty in the measurements stems from the background estimation. The results are in accordance with the predictions of the Standard Model calculations.
